# Version source of truth

The Keel version's major, minor, and patch come from git tags (`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`). The build is the short commit hash. The visible form is `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH+<short hash>`.

- Read it at runtime with `keel.version.package_version()` (installed distribution metadata filled from git by `setuptools-scm`).
- Do not write the version as a string in `pyproject.toml`, Python, HTML, tests, ADRs, or README.
- `.github/initial-version` is the only seed, and only for publishing the first tag when the repository has none.
- Tests must assert against `package_version()`, not a copied version number.
- After a new git tag, reinstall (`pip install -e ".[dev]"`) so metadata updates.

See `docs/version.md` and `docs/adr/version-from-git-tags.md`. The footer display remains ADR 002.
